# AntennaTracker defaults for the camera towers.
#
# PITCH_MIN/PITCH_MAX must match the tilt joint limits in terrain/tower.py.
# ArduPilot maps its full servo range onto this span, and the Gazebo plugin
# maps that same servo range onto the joint range -- so if the two disagree the
# tracker either cannot reach its limits or grinds against a hard stop.
#
# Positive pitch is up in ArduPilot; the joint's positive direction is down.
# -70 keeps the camera out of its own mast, +45 is enough to follow an aircraft
# overhead without the head folding back on the fork.
PITCH_MIN -70
PITCH_MAX 45
YAW_RANGE 360

# SITL has no calibrated accels or compass, so the stock prearm set can never
# pass. A tower has no propulsion to make safe.
ARMING_CHECK 0

# Boot into MANUAL, not AUTO.
#
# AUTO with no tracked vehicle emits PWM 0 on both channels. SIM_Gazebo
# normalises PWM as (pwm-1000)/1000, so 0 becomes a command of -1.0, and the
# plugin's target = multiplier*(offset+cmd) then lands far outside the joint
# range. The position loop grinds against the hard stop and the whole head
# buzzes. MANUAL holds 1500/1500 -- pan centred, tilt mid-range -- and takes
# pan/tilt commands over MAVLink, which is what a camera tower wants anyway.
# Switch to AUTO from a GCS once there is a vehicle to track.
INITIAL_MODE 0
